## Slot vocabulary ({{slot-count}} slots inherited or declared)

Predicate memorials inherit `:mm/Memory` plus type-specific required slots:

- **`domain`** — set of type-memorial rel-paths the predicate accepts as source
- **`range`** — set of type-memorial rel-paths the predicate accepts as target
- **`characteristics`** — set of formal properties (transitive / reflexive / irreflexive / symmetric / antisymmetric / asymmetric / functional / inverse-functional)
- **`inverse-of`** — the dagger-dual predicate, if any
- **`same-type?`** / **`acyclic?`** — additional formal constraints
- **`lifecycle-status`** — `active` / `deprecated` / `retired` / `candidate`
- **`prefer-over`** / **`reach-for-instead`** — relative-strength guidance

